\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Deepen the wound Thy hands have made
\par In this weak, helpless soul;
\par Till mercy, with its kindly aid,
\par Descends to make me whole.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. The sharpness of Thy two-edged sword
\par Enable me to endure;
\par Till bold to say: My hallowing Lord
\par Hath wrought a perfect cure.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. I see the exceeding broad command,
\par Which all contains in one:
\par Enlarge my heart to understand
\par The mystery unknown.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. O that with all the saints I might
\par By sweet experience prove
\par What is the length, and breadth, and height,
\par And depth of perfect love!\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

